# SQL vs NoSQL - Real-World Company Examples

> **Note:** Many large companies use **both SQL and NoSQL** databases depending on the problem they're solving.

## Companies Using Both SQL & NoSQL

| Company | SQL | NoSQL | Why |
|---------|:---:|:------:|-----|
| Amazon | ✅ | ✅ | Orders and payments use SQL; shopping carts and recommendations often use NoSQL. |
| Netflix | ✅ | ✅ | Uses SQL for transactional data and NoSQL for streaming metadata and scalability. |
| Facebook | ✅ | ✅ | SQL for some internal systems; NoSQL for massive social graph and messaging data. |
| Google | ✅ | ✅ | Uses SQL databases and large-scale NoSQL systems for search and cloud services. |
| Uber | ✅ | ✅ | SQL for trips and payments; NoSQL for location and high-volume operational data. |
| Airbnb | ✅ | ✅ | SQL manages bookings; NoSQL helps with caching and fast lookups. |
| Spotify | ✅ | ✅ | SQL stores user and subscription data; NoSQL helps with playlists and recommendations. |
| LinkedIn | ✅ | ✅ | SQL for member accounts; NoSQL for feeds and large-scale data. |

# Class 12
# CRUD in the Real World

## What is CRUD?

CRUD stands for the four basic actions applications perform on data.

- **C** = Create
- **R** = Read
- **U** = Update
- **D** = Delete

Almost every website or app uses CRUD.

---

# Real-World Examples

## 🛒 Online Shopping (Amazon)

### Create
- Add a new product
- Create a customer account
- Place an order

### Read
- View products
- Read product reviews
- Check order history

### Update
- Change shipping address
- Update payment method
- Edit shopping cart

### Delete
- Remove an item from the cart
- Delete a saved payment method

---

## 🏦 Banking App

### Create
- Open a new account
- Add a new payee

### Read
- View account balance
- View transaction history

### Update
- Change contact information
- Update account settings

### Delete
- Remove a scheduled payment
- Close an account

---

## 📚 Library System

### Create
- Add a new book
- Register a new member

### Read
- Search for books
- View available copies

### Update
- Edit book information
- Renew a checkout

### Delete
- Remove damaged books
- Delete inactive member accounts

---

## 🎵 Spotify

### Create
- Create a playlist
- Upload a podcast

### Read
- Browse artists
- View playlists

### Update
- Rename a playlist
- Change playlist order

### Delete
- Delete a playlist
- Remove a saved song

---

## 💬 Social Media

### Create
- Create a post
- Upload a photo
- Write a comment

### Read
- View posts
- Read comments
- Browse profiles

### Update
- Edit a post
- Change profile information

### Delete
- Delete a post
- Remove a comment

